<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="GEOL 100" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2007" href="schedule/2007.xml">2007</calendarYear><term id="120078" href="schedule/2007/fall.xml">Fall 2007</term><subject id="GEOL" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL.xml">Geology</subject></parents><label>Planet Earth</label><description>Introduces non-science majors to physical aspects (earthquakes, volcanoes, floods, tsunamis, mountains, plate tectonics) and historical aspects (formation of earth and life, dinosaurs, ice age, evolution of climate) in earth science. Presents information on earth resources, natural hazards, and development of natural landscapes. Focuses on humanistic issues; provides context for understanding environmental change. Optional lab demonstrations and field trips with co-registration in GEOL 110. Credit is not given for both GEOL 100 and GEOL 101, GEOL 103, GEOL 107, or GEOL 111. </description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sectionDegreeAttributes>Physical Sciences course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="NAT"><description>Natural Sciences &amp; Technology</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1PS">Nat Sci &amp; Tech - Phys Sciences</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="37467" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37467.xml">AD1</section><section id="37469" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37469.xml">AD2</section><section id="37470" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37470.xml">ADA</section><section id="37471" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37471.xml">ADB</section><section id="37472" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37472.xml">ADC</section><section id="37473" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37473.xml">ADD</section><section id="37474" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37474.xml">ADE</section><section id="37475" href="schedule/2007/fall/GEOL/100/37475.xml">ADF<